# npm 10.9.4's arborist crashes resolving peer dependencies across these workspaces:
#   TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')
#   at #loadPeerSet (build-ideal-tree.js:1289), while resolving node_modules/vitest
#
# It reproduces on a completely clean tree (all node_modules deleted), so it is not
# stale state — it is npm's peer-set recursion, triggered by hoisting vitest across
# the frontend and backend workspaces (both declare vitest ^4.1.8).
#
# TRADE-OFF: this disables peer-conflict detection repo-wide. npm will no longer warn
# when a package's peer requirements are genuinely unsatisfiable, so incompatibilities
# surface at runtime instead of install time. Revisit when npm is upgraded — test by
# removing this file and running `npm install` on a clean tree.
legacy-peer-deps=true
